# The authority that published this deployment's ladder presets. Without it
# the app labels every config as third-party and never offers to create one.
# `bun run configs:init` prints the value to use.
VITE_TAPER_ADMIN=

# The endpoint this deployment ships with. Pool and position browsing is
# getProgramAccounts, which the public devnet endpoint rate-limits per IP, so a
# busy page hits 429 part way through a list and looks broken.
#
# Whatever goes here is baked into the JS bundle and is public to anyone who
# opens the app, so a paid endpoint put here is a shared quota with a key you
# can only revoke by rotating. A visitor can point their own browser at their
# own endpoint from the RPC chip in the header, which is stored locally and
# needs no rebuild.
#
# `bun run dev` proxies this through the Vite server (`/rpc/devnet`) instead of
# letting the page call it cross-origin, so an endpoint that mishandles the CORS
# preflight still works locally and its key never enters the dev bundle. A
# production build has no proxy: check that a deployed endpoint answers OPTIONS
# with `access-control-allow-origin` before shipping it here.
VITE_DEVNET_RPC=https://api.devnet.solana.com
VITE_LOCALNET_RPC=http://127.0.0.1:8899
